./LOGBOOK.md:408:- DECISION: **Ceremony C1 shrank.** No App Group record is created and the App Groups capability is enabled on no App ID. The convenience argument did not need weighing — it evaporates: C1's `explicitlyNotAuthorized` already excludes all four iOS App IDs under ADR-024, so iOS provisioning *already* needs a later portal sitting, and those four iOS App IDs are the records' only consumers. New rule **R30** makes C1 scope **derived** from what its App IDs require, so growing or shrinking it by hand cannot pass.
./LOGBOOK.md:431:- BLOCKED: Nothing. Named limitation instead — `sudo -n true` exit 1 in a non-interactive session, so **no code was run as root**. Checks V1–V3 (V1 System keychain write from the signed sandboxed provider, V2 root group-container path, V3 system start with the app not running) were appended to `TASK-260715-9yp8to` rather than creating a duplicate physical-Mac node (ADR-028a). r2 added **V4/V5** to the same node.
./LOGBOOK.md:434:- ROOT CAUSE: r2 argued in D-4 that `ReluxProxyMac` is sandboxed *because of* Sparkle, and quoted the spec clause naming the `-spks`/`-spki` Mach lookup exceptions — then never authored `com.apple.security.temporary-exception.mach-lookup.global-name` as an entitlement row. The r2 containment assertion A10b declares every present key must be authored or signing-generated, so the allowlist would have **rejected a correctly built sandboxed Sparkle host**. Same defect class as r1's F3, one revision later: prose acknowledged the requirement, the machine-checkable set did not. The generalisable lesson is that the moment an assertion becomes *exhaustive*, every architectural consequence stated anywhere in the contract must also appear as data — rationale text is no longer a place a requirement can live.
./LOGBOOK.md:438:- DECISION: The row is attributed `project-architecture`, **not** `sandbox-consequence`, even though `com.apple.security.network.client` on the same target is a sandbox consequence and is equally Sparkle-driven. `network.client` follows mechanically from sandboxing alone; this key needs two independent project decisions to both hold (ADR-018's Sparkle choice **and** the host sandbox), so it is not derivable from "this target is sandboxed". Also added **rule X1**: the spec bans "unreviewed exception entitlement", so the contract now carries a reviewed-exception register plus an explicit banned set for Hardened Runtime relaxations — `get-task-allow` deliberately excluded from that set, since it is toolchain-injected on the development channel and governed by A10d instead. Without X1 this defect recurs one key at a time.
./LOGBOOK.md:442:- ROOT CAUSE: The r1 matrix assigned `packet-tunnel-provider-systemextension` to all four macOS targets unconditionally while authorizing **Mac Development** profiles for the same four App IDs. Apple DTS is explicit that the value follows the distribution channel: the `-systemextension` suffix is for direct Developer ID signing, and "otherwise — including when you distribute the app on the App Store and when signing for development — use the values without that suffix" (forums/thread/800887). Ceremony C1 would have provisioned development profiles against a value development signing never uses, and C1 is a one-shot human node (ADR-028).
./LOGBOOK.md:448:- DECISION: `ReluxProxyMac`'s sandbox is recorded as a **project** decision — `.spec/platform-distribution.md` embeds Sparkle only in the sandboxed hardened-runtime host with `SUEnableInstallerLauncherService` and the `-spks`/`-spki` Mach exceptions, per ADR-018 — not an Apple rule. The contract now carries `requirementSource` per row (`apple-requirement` / `project-architecture` / `sandbox-consequence` / `platform-inherent`) and validator R21 rejects a host row claiming an Apple requirement.
./LOGBOOK.md:457:### 0718 — A containment assertion that ignores signing-generated entitlements is unrunnable (TASK-260715-ypo7yo, r2)
./LOGBOOK.md:471:- FINDING: The generated target *names* from `.spec/platform-distribution.md` are `ReluxProxyMac`/`ReluxProxyIOS`. Any generator that derives a bundle identifier from the target name emits `works.relux.proxy.mac` — inside the shipped legacy `works.relux.proxy` identity namespace, which is exactly the silent-repurposing failure AC4 forbids. Target name and bundle identifier are explicitly decoupled and assertion A11 (`^works\.relux\.proxy(\.|$)`) exists to catch it.
./LOGBOOK.md:473:- FINDING: Probe identifiers had to be in this matrix, not invented later by `1r0fxv`. C1 authorizes "exactly the approved macOS entries"; had the probe been absent, provisioning it would have needed a second human sitting — the thing ADR-028 forbids.
./LOGBOOK.md:491:- ANOMALY: Round 2 described Ceremony C1 as one sitting, but no board element owned the sitting. The four grant-bearing tasks were ordered `apc34w` → {`3jloqy`, `dveo1o`}, so a `max_parallel = 1` scheduler produced **two** human stops with a full producer→reviewer cycle between them. Prose cannot batch a human interaction; only the DAG can. Recorded as ADR-028 and fixed by creating `TASK-260728-q5kjta`, the single up-front human-input node; `apc34w`, `3jloqy`, `dveo1o`, `ziprhs` are now unattended agent evidence tasks behind it, with their evidence obligations intact.
./LOGBOOK.md:494:- FINDING: The board diff contained **75** removed dependency edges (37 task-to-task, 38 container), not the 17 round 2 reported. The 38 container removals were `task-board repair-links` clearing unsupported container links that also carried four container-level cycles; 34 of them are still enforced at task level, and the 4 that are not are intentional A0/ADR-011 deferrals. Full per-edge ledger with retained-counterpart proofs is attached to the task.
./LOGBOOK.md:500:- ANOMALY: A deferred task left in `backlog` with its blockers removed is **schedulable**. Deferring iOS/A0/NIOSSH by unlinking their edges made 15 prohibited elements eligible — `TASK-260715-1af33i` (NIOSSH adapter, forbidden by ADR-014) landed in Wave 1 of the "autonomous" run. Board validation was green throughout. Recorded as ADR-027: deferral is expressed as `blocked` status with an evidence packet, never as an unlinked backlog item.
./LOGBOOK.md:504:- FINDING: The notarization credential was described as "available" while existing only as a mode-0600 `.p8` file — the project invariant is Keychain-only. ADR-025 now requires a named `notarytool` Keychain profile, a real authentication check, and a recorded disposition for the source file; `TASK-260728-dveo1o` owns it and blocks `3gkwn0`.
./LOGBOOK.md:505:- DECISION: Sparkle key generation separated from updater integration (ADR-026). `ziprhs` may run at C1 because it depends on nothing; `SUPublicEDKey` pinning and appcast sign/verify became `TASK-260728-3bj9bk`, blocked by `uyju7n` → `xempiv` and `1mt4e7`. Accepting the key ceremony no longer implies a working self-update signing path.
./LOGBOOK.md:506:- FINDING: `TASK-260715-32umrc` (generated-project architecture ADR) is blocked by `2ayxqn` (Gate P0). That is why only 35 tasks precede the ceremony — an ADR-011 gate deliberately kept, not a graph defect. Schedule C1 early and run segment 1 alongside arranging it.
./LOGBOOK.md:512:- DECISION: Owner-approved strategy encoded in `.spec/decisions.md` as ADR-023 (M0 SSH viability scope, Option A, with the four deferred semantics named and owned by TASK-260728-3cveay) and ADR-024 (macOS-only physical target, iOS deferred, Linux CI nonblocking, Relux Works signing/notary available). ADR-013 re-scoped from a blocking prototype gate to a release-path gate; ADR-014 moved Open → Accepted with libssh2 as the primary engine.
./LOGBOOK.md:572:- GATE: DNS candidate limits remain non-authoritative with `productionAuthorization.permitted=false`. Production use still requires accepted selected-SSH `direct-tcpip` timing/footprint/cleanup evidence (`TASK-260715-1gjxer`), the ADR-009 residual DNS component budget (`TASK-260715-1pn983`), physical-provider startup/footprint rows, and independent review.
./LOGBOOK.md:601:- REWORK: Clean and incremental preparation plus environment construction now lstat the workspace root and every HOME/cache child, reject symlinks and other non-directory types with exact diagnostics, and require resolved child paths to remain below the resolved target sandbox. Regression coverage preserves clean deletion and legitimate incremental reuse while closing the external-cache escape.
./LOGBOOK.md:701:- IMPLEMENTATION: The authoritative standard-library-only relay module now pins Go 1.26.5 and builds `relux-relay` plus `relux-relay-protocol-test` for Darwin/Linux amd64/arm64. Both expose deterministic credential-free metadata smoke output; the protocol-test entry point runs only empty health and one generated-schema-backed version mismatch, and the relay explicitly reports that feature behavior is not implemented.
./LOGBOOK.md:717:- RELIABILITY/CLEANUP: Event traces now cover both IPv4→IPv6 and IPv6→IPv4 orders, cancellation/tombstone/late-response races, duplicate attempts before suppression, every M2 fallback trigger, malformed/mismatched no-shopping, same-endpoint TCP, later promotion, and exact attempt/terminal counts. Transactions, queue bytes, reservations, tombstones, connections, connection buffers, fixed bytes, and descriptors return to observed zero after every regenerated run.
