@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+# TASK-260715-2btjwm — workspace foundation results
+
+## Outcome
+
+Ready for independent review. The repository now generates
+`ReluxTunnel.xcworkspace` and `ReluxTunnelApp.xcodeproj` from source-controlled
+Tuist manifests using exactly Tuist 4.202.5 through Mise. Generated Xcode state
+and the credential-bearing local signing overlay are ignored.
+
+The foundation defines exactly Debug and Release, one shared settings chain,
+macOS 15.0 and iOS 18.0 inputs, Swift 6 complete-concurrency inputs, provider
+extension-safe overlays, credential-free signing defaults, the accepted r12
+identifier projection, and one version input. It exposes exactly the eight ADR
+scheme names; deferred iOS schemes are hidden. Automatic project/workspace
+schemes are disabled so dependent target tasks extend stable names.
+
+The existing root `Package.swift` remains tracked and byte-unchanged. The
+generated project contains an Xcode local-package reference to `.` and does not
+absorb package sources or tests.
+
+## Source-controlled deliverables
+
+- `mise.toml`, `Tuist.swift`, `Workspace.swift`, and `Project.swift`
+- `Configuration/*.xcconfig` checked-in settings, identity, version, provider,
+  and signing-example inputs
+- `scripts/generate-workspace.sh` pinned clean generator
+- `scripts/validate-workspace-foundation.sh` normalized double-generation gate
+- `Makefile` entry points: `workspace-generate`, `workspace-validate`
+- `docs/generated-workspace-foundation.md` and updated README tool inventory
+- `.gitignore` generated-project and local-signing policy
+
+## Validation evidence
+
+All commands were run from `/Users/iv/Developer/relux-tunnel`.
+
+- `mise exec -- tuist version` — exit 0, output `4.202.5`.
+- `make workspace-validate` — exit 0. Two clean generations had identical
+  normalized file hashes; exactly eight Xcode schemes were visible; Debug and
+  Release, deployment/Swift/signing/version/provider inputs, ignored generated
+  state, local-package reference, and Package.swift preservation passed.
+- `swift format lint Project.swift Tuist.swift Workspace.swift` — exit 0,
+  no diagnostics.
+- `sh -n scripts/generate-workspace.sh scripts/validate-workspace-foundation.sh`
+  — exit 0.
+- `swift test` — exit 0; 443 tests in 37 suites passed with 25 pre-existing
+  recorded known issues.
+- `swift build` — exit 0.
+- `git diff --check` — exit 0.
+
+Task-scoped logs: `.temp/TASK-260715-2btjwm/validate-foundation-05.log`,
+`swift-test-01.log`, `swift-build-01.log`, `swift-format-04.log`,
+`tuist-version-01.log`, `generation-01.sha256`, `generation-02.sha256`, and
+`xcodebuild-list.log`.
+
+## Findings and expected behavior
+
+Mise initially rejected the new repository config as untrusted (exit 1). After
+the documented one-time `mise trust mise.toml`, installation and pinned
+generation succeeded. Tuist/Xcode reports that the foundation schemes have no
+supported build destination because this task intentionally adds no platform
+targets or source. This is expected and is resolved when the dependent host,
+provider, package-action, and relay-action tasks attach build/test actions to
+the stable schemes; it is not reported as a build pass for those future targets.
